    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0490" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg486"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163P92/144: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-01T17:00:00+08:00">October 1, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 1—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1285. Department’s 562, September 30, 8 p.m., and this office’s 1226, September
                    15, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d655-f1"/> properties of American Presbyterian
                    Mission North at Soochow occupied by Japanese. A telegram has just been received
                    from Crawford, mission representative at Soochow, reading as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Presbyterian properties fully returned, badly damaged.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Code texts of this telegram and the Department’s 562, September 30, 8 p.m., are
                    being sent by mail to Chungking, Peiping and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d655-f1" n="2" xml:id="d655-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
